              −12 
              {eV}, can change the probability that a molecule-surface collision will stop a molecule from rotating and lose rotational energy which is 9 orders larger than that of the magnetic manipulation. Calculations confirm that different rotational orientations have different de-excitation probabilities but underestimate rotational flips (∆
              m
              
                J
              
              
                
                  \$\${\textbackslash}ne\$\$
                  
                    ≠
                  
                
              
