	abstract = {A polarized atomic beam source was developed for the polarized internal storage-cell gas target at the magnet spectrometer {ANKE} of {COSY}-Jülich. The intensities of the beams injected into the storage cell, measured with a compression tube, are \$7.5{\textbackslash}cdot 10{\textasciicircum}\{16\}\$ hydrogen atoms/s (two hyperfine states) and \$3.9{\textbackslash}cdot 10{\textasciicircum}\{16\}\$ deuterium atoms/s (three hyperfine states). For the hydrogen beam the achieved vector polarizations are \$p\_\{{\textbackslash}rm z\}{\textbackslash}approx{\textbackslash}pm0.92\$. For the deuterium beam, the obtained combinations of vector and tensor (\$p\_\{{\textbackslash}rm zz\}\$) polarizations are \$p\_\{{\textbackslash}rm z\}{\textbackslash}approx{\textbackslash}pm 0.90\$ (with a constant \$p\_\{{\textbackslash}rm zz\}{\textbackslash}approx +0.86\$), and \$p\_\{{\textbackslash}rm zz\}=+0.90\$ or \$p\_\{{\textbackslash}rm zz\}=-1.71\$ (both with vanishing \$p\_\{{\textbackslash}rm z\}\$). The paper includes a detailed technical description of the apparatus and of the investigations performed during the development.},
